# package shapes

A package comment opens the package's page.

## Point

```odin
Point :: struct {
	// Across, in metres.
	x: f64,
	y: f64,
	// and fields private to the package
}
```

A point on the plane.

## Handle

```odin
Handle :: struct {
	// and fields private to the package
}
```

Opaque to importers.

## Facing

```odin
Facing :: enum { North, South }
```

The directions a shape may face.

## MAX_SIDE

```odin
MAX_SIDE :: 1000
```

The largest side any shape may have.

## make_point

```odin
make_point :: proc(x: f64, y: f64) -> Point
```

## limit

```odin
limit := 10
```

## square_area

```odin
@(require_results)
square_area :: proc(side: f64) -> f64
```

The area of a square with `side`.
It is always non-negative.

## Point.sum

```odin
sum :: proc(self) -> f64
```

The sum of the coordinates.

## LONGEST

```odin
LONGEST :: units.METRE * MAX_SIDE
```

The longest side, in metres.

# package units (`./units`)

Lengths, in metres. `-doc` gives each package of the project its own page,
after the root's.

## METRE

```odin
METRE :: 1.0
```

One metre.
